---
import BlogPost from '$lib/layouts/BlogPost.astro';

export const title = 'CrofAI is an OpenRouter wrapper';
export const date = '2026-09-13';
---

<BlogPost {title} {date}>
  <p>
    <strong
      ><a href="https://crof.ai">CrofAI</a> accepts the <code>openrouter:advisor</code> tool</strong
    >, completely unexpected for an independent inference provider. Recording the results of using
    this tool across every model shows <strong
      >CrofAI is an OpenRouter wrapper that silently routes to cheaper or weaker models than what
      you request</strong
    >, explaining its low prices. Proof that this was true at the time of writing follows later.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong
      >These models are routed to <a href="https://openrouter.ai/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731"
        >DeepSeek V4 Flash 0731</a
      >:</strong
    >
  </p>
